*.mp4
output/
build/

# Python bytecode. pvbatch and the VisIt CLI both leave it beside the scripts
# they import, and `python -m py_compile` scatters it further.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# VisIt writes a transcript of the session next to whatever it ran.
visitlog.py

# Fetched once by data/fetchData.sh, 4.3 GB, and already extracted beside it.
data/KAUST_Visualization_Vignettes_Large_Data.zip

# Per-run artifacts written into each vignette's Testing/ directory. This is
# the same set test_suite.py --clean removes, and none of it is an input to
# anything. Two things under Testing/ ARE inputs and are deliberately not
# ignored: Baseline/ (the blessed baselines) and performance_metrics_*.json
# (the committed history that makes long-term comparison possible).
*/*/Testing/output.log
*/*/Testing/error.log
*/*/Testing/run_result.json
*/*/Testing/image_comparison_results.json
*/*/Testing/text_comparison_results.json
*/*/Testing/results_comparison.json
*/*/Testing/csv_comparison_results.json
*/*/Testing/*_results.json
!*/*/Testing/Baseline/*_results.json
*/*/Testing/execution_time_*.png
*/*/Testing/cpu_usage_*.png
*/*/Testing/memory_usage_*.png
*/combined_execution_time_plot.png
Testing/*_summary_report.json

# Generated locally by Testing/prepare_machine.py, never committed. Every one
# of these is version-locked, path-locked, or both, and none of them announces
# a mismatch: an AMR hierarchy written by ParaView 6.1.0 opens under 6.0.1 and
# quietly reads 216 points where 842 were written, and a VisIt .session from
# the wrong version restores with plots silently missing. Regenerating on each
# machine is cheap; discovering this in a queue is not.
#
#     python3 Testing/prepare_machine.py --check
#
VisIt_Vignettes/ex11_visitStateVerification/ex11_visit.session
VisIt_Vignettes/ex11_visitStateVerification/ex11_series.visit
ParaView_Vignettes/ex11_pvStateVerification/ex11_state.pvsm
data/topologies/
data/varying_series_xml/

# Fetched by data/fetchData.sh alongside the zip, 4.3 GB extracted.
data/currentRainfall.silo
data/cyclone-chapala-2015-11-02_00-00-00-mb.vtm
data/cyclone-chapala-2015-11-02_00-00-00-mb/

# Scratch space for one-off comparison sheets and backups. Never an input.
.scratch/

# Wheels collected by Testing/make_offline_bundle.sh for an air-gapped
# machine. 52 MB of binaries that pip can rebuild in a minute.
offline_bundle/

# Per-user editor state. The LTeX dictionaries in here are one person's
# spelling preferences, not a repository setting.
.vscode/

# Local build and install trees kept inside the working copy for convenience.
# Nothing under them is tracked, they are ~99 GB and ~185,000 files between
# them, and they are what makes a bare `git status` here take minutes. Ignored
# rather than moved out so everything stays in one folder, and so that one
# `git add -A` cannot commit a compiler's output.
software/
Miniapps/gray-scott/install/
Miniapps/gray-scott/local_tests/
Miniapps/gray-scott/shaheenDownload/
